  "solution": {
    "approach": "Using two heaps, a max heap to store the smaller half of the numbers and a min heap to store the larger half of the numbers.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(log N) for adding a number and O(1) for finding the median",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(N) for storing the numbers in the heaps",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#define MAX 100000\n#define MIN -100000\n// max heap and min heap implementation",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\n#include <queue>\nusing namespace std;\npriority_queue<int> maxHeap;\npriority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> minHeap;",
      "Java": "import java.util.PriorityQueue;\npublic class MedianFinder {\n    PriorityQueue<Integer> maxHeap = new PriorityQueue<>((a, b) -> b - a);\n    PriorityQueue<Integer> minHeap = new PriorityQueue<>();",
      "Python3": "import heapq\n\nclass MedianFinder:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.maxHeap = []\n        self.minHeap = []",
      "JavaScript": "class MedianFinder {\n    constructor() {\n        this.maxHeap = [];\n        this.minHeap = [];\n    }\n}"
